## 7. Example of Compressed Line Information

Suppose six consecutive bytes have these source line numbers:

```text
Byte offset:   0  1  2  3  4  5
Source line:   7  7  7  7  8  8
```

The original implementation stores:

```text
[7, 7, 7, 7, 8, 8]
```

The compressed implementation only stores:

```text
LineStart { offset: 0, line: 7 }
LineStart { offset: 4, line: 8 }
```

The getLine() function retrieves the correct line for each byte offset.

For example:

```c
getLine(&chunk, 0); // Returns 7
getLine(&chunk, 2); // Returns 7
getLine(&chunk, 4); // Returns 8
getLine(&chunk, 5); // Returns 8
```

